      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 27
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Two known gaps\n\n**Errors are not attributable.** `ai-statistics` emits seven counters and none carries a status code, so the status panel to the left is gateway-wide. \"Which consumer is getting 422s\" cannot be answered from Prometheus at all today.\n\n**Latency has no tail.** The TTFT panel is a mean over a windowed count. A single 40-second request among a hundred fast ones does not move it \u2014 and that is the request people complain about.\n\nBoth close in **Stage B**, when the gateway access log (already carrying `request_id`, tokens, status and duration per request) gains a `consumer` field and is tailed into ClickHouse.\n\n**Also:** balances are exact and durable; spend and share are not. Envoy counters reset on a gateway restart, so anything derived from them under-reports across one. Invoices read the balance."
      }
